(>> 2.1 CSS3 Syntax, Cascading Rules and Specificity Hierarchy) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Cascading Style Sheets \(CSS3\) dictates the presentation, layout, visual aesthetics, and) Tj
T*
(responsive behavior of HTML documents across display viewports.) Tj
T*
(* CSS Syntax: selector { property: value; }.) Tj
T*
(* Insertion Methods: \(1\) Inline Styles \(<h1 style='...'>\) - highest specificity,) Tj
T*
(violates separation of concerns. \(2\) Internal Stylesheet \(<style> in <head>\). \(3\)) Tj
T*
(External Stylesheet \(<link rel='stylesheet' href='style.css'>\) - industry standard,) Tj
T*
(enables browser caching.) Tj
T*
(* The Cascade and Specificity Hierarchy: When conflicting rules target an element,) Tj
T*
(the browser computes Specificity Scores represented as \(Inline, IDs,) Tj
T*
(Classes/Attributes/Pseudo-classes, Elements/Pseudo-elements\):) Tj
T*
(- Inline style: \(1, 0, 0, 0\) = Score 1000.) Tj
T*
(- ID selector \(#header\): \(0, 1, 0, 0\) = Score 100.) Tj
T*
(- Class, attribute, pseudo-class \(.btn, [type='text'], :hover\): \(0, 0, 1, 0\) = Score 10.) Tj
T*
(- Element, pseudo-element \(p, h1, ::before\): \(0, 0, 0, 1\) = Score 1.) Tj
T*
(- Universal selector \(*\), combinators \(+, >, ~\): \(0, 0, 0, 0\) = Score 0.) Tj
T*
(- The !important override trumps all specificity, but should be avoided to prevent) Tj
T*
(unmaintainable code.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.2 The CSS Box Model and Sizing Paradigms) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Every rendered HTML element is treated as a rectangular box comprising four concentric) Tj
T*
(layers:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Content: The actual text, image, or media content area \(width x height\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Padding: Transparent interior clearance between content and border.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Border: Structural perimeter line wrapping padding and content.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Margin: Transparent exterior clearance separating the element from neighboring) Tj
T*
(boxes.) Tj
T*
(* The Critical box-sizing Property:) Tj
T*
(- content-box \(Default\): Total Width = width + padding_left + padding_right +) Tj
T*
(border_left + border_right. Adding padding increases physical element size, frequently) Tj
T*
(breaking grid layouts.) Tj
T*
(- border-box \(Universal Best Practice\): Total Width = declared width. Padding and border) Tj
T*
(are absorbed inside the declared width: * { box-sizing: border-box; }.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

