(>> 2.6 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Contrast the CSS Box Model under 'box-sizing: content-box' versus 'box-sizing:) Tj
T*
(border-box' with a numerical dimension calculation.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Under 'content-box' \(CSS default\), declared width and height apply strictly to) Tj
T*
(the content box. Total rendered width is calculated as: Width_total = width +) Tj
T*
(padding_left + padding_right + border_left + border_right. For an element with width:) Tj
T*
(300px, padding: 20px, and border: 5px, Total Width = 300 + 20 + 20 + 5 + 5 = 350px. If) Tj
T*
(placed inside a 300px parent column, it overflows and breaks the layout. Under) Tj
T*
('box-sizing: border-box', the declared width includes content, padding, and border. The) Tj
T*
(browser automatically compresses content width: Content Width = 300 - \(40 + 10\) = 250px.) Tj
T*
(Total rendered width remains exactly 300px, guaranteeing layout stability.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: When should a web developer select CSS Flexbox versus CSS Grid? Detail their) Tj
T*
(architectural differences.) Tj
T*
(Answer: The fundamental distinction is dimensional scope: \(1\) Flexbox is) Tj
T*
(One-Dimensional: It manages layout along a single axis at a time \(either row OR column\).) Tj
T*
(It is content-driven \(items determine their own width/flex distribution\) and is optimal) Tj
T*
(for interface components such as navigation menus, button groups, form input rows, and) Tj
T*
(centering elements. \(2\) CSS Grid is Two-Dimensional: It manages rows AND columns) Tj
T*
(simultaneously. It is layout-driven \(the container establishes rigid structural tracks) Tj
T*
(into which elements are placed\) and is optimal for overarching page architectures,) Tj
T*
(complex dashboards, multi-column image galleries, and overlapping component grids.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.7 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Specificity formula: Inline \(1000\) > ID \(100\) > Class \(10\) > Element \(1\).) Tj
T*
(* Always set box-sizing: border-box universally across all elements.) Tj
T*
(* Flexbox manages 1D alignments \(main vs cross axis\); CSS Grid controls 2D rows and) Tj
T*
(columns.) Tj
T*
(* repeat\(auto-fit, minmax\(min, 1fr\)\) creates responsive grids without media queries.) Tj
T*
ET

